Data Collection Pipeline

The repository contains a dedicated data_collection_pipeline

directory.

Its major areas are:


data_collection_pipeline/

├── mapping/

├── qco/

├── regulatory/

├── scraper/

├── download_documents.py

├── organize_products.py

└── requirements.txt


Scraper

The scraper package contains modules for:

  API access

  Browser-assisted collection

  Collection orchestration

  Downloading

  Storage

  Organization

Mapping

The mapping package contains modules for:

  Product loading

  Standard mapping

  QCO mapping

  Regulatory mapping

  Normalization

  Confidence handling

  Relationship building

  Export

Document Downloader

download_documents.py can inspect BIS JSON records, discover document

references and download referenced documents from the BIS document

server.

Downloaded documents are accompanied by a manifest containing download

status and metadata.

RAG Pipeline

The main indexing implementation is:


RAG/index.py


It performs:

 Qdrant connection.

 Collection creation.

 Standard-to-product mapping.

 JSON extraction.

 Structured record enrichment.

 PDF text extraction.

 Chunking.

 Embedding generation.

 Batch vector upload.

Current indexing configuration:


Embedding model : all-MiniLM-L6-v2

Chunk size      : 1000

Overlap         : 200

Distance        : COSINE

Collection      : bis_knowledge

Qdrant          : http://localhost:6333


Structured records are enriched with metadata. Laboratory and licence

records are represented differently from large PDF documents.

Important: machine-specific data path

The current RAG/index.py contains:


DATA_DIR = Path(r"D:\SIH2026\data_collection_pipeline\data")


After cloning the repository on another computer, update this path to

the actual dataset location before rebuilding the index.

Index rebuild warning

The indexer recreates the bis_knowledge Qdrant collection. Treat

python RAG/index.py as a rebuild operation rather than a harmless

incremental update.

Retrieval

The primary retrieval implementation is:


RAG/chat.py


It provides semantic Qdrant search plus structured laboratory retrieval.

The retrieval layer includes:

  Query embedding

  Similarity search

  Product filtering

  Metadata filtering

  Deduplication

  Document compaction

  Context construction

  Exhaustive laboratory retrieval

Large documents are compacted while small structured laboratory records

can be preserved more completely.

Deterministic Retrieval

A key engineering principle is:

Not every question should be answered by an LLM.

Normal knowledge question:


Question

   ↓

Semantic Retrieval

   ↓

Relevant Context

   ↓

LLM


Exhaustive/count/list question:


Count/List Question

        ↓

Exhaustive Record Retrieval

        ↓

Product/Standard Filtering

        ↓

Deduplication

        ↓

Python Calculation

        ↓

Exact Result


This is useful for questions where an LLM should not be trusted to count

or enumerate records from a small retrieved context.

Query Understanding

The main query-understanding module is:


jagruk_brain_pipeline/input_processor.py


It acts as a preprocessing layer.

Its responsibilities include:

  Understanding the user's question

  Detecting language

  Mapping supported common product names

  Identifying intent

  Producing retrieval search terms

  Creating a dense retrieval query

  Preserving the user's language for final response generation

Example:


User:

"Pressure cooker ka BIS standard kya hai?"

        ↓

Language:

Romanized Hindi / Hinglish

        ↓

Product:

Domestic Pressure Cooker

        ↓

Intent:

Standard lookup

        ↓

Retrieval Query:

Pressure cooker BIS standard specification


LangGraph Pipeline

The orchestration entry point is:


jagruk_brain_pipeline/main.py


Pipeline state contains values such as:


medium

raw_query

detected_language

filtered_query

final_answer


Conceptually:


START

  │

  ▼

Input Medium

  │

  ├──────── Text ──────────┐

  │                        │

  └──────── Voice ──→ STT ─┘

